// The harmonik workspace ties the existing root module together with the new
// segment modules of the platform re-grounding. Each segment is its own module,
// so one segment cannot reach into another segment's internal packages — the
// wall is the compiler, not a naming rule.
//
// Members, and only these four:
//   .            the existing root module (the live daemon; unchanged).
//   ./contract   the wire contract (a pure leaf).
//   ./kernel     the substrate.
//   ./tools/echo the first tool.
//
// Layout of record: plans/2026-09-07-harmonik-restructure/
//   07-segmented-structure-and-day1-standards.md and 06-segmented-layout.md.
// There is no shared/ module yet: shared admits a package only when a second
// consumer exists in committed code, and none does today.

go 1.25

toolchain go1.26.3

use (
	.
	./contract
	./kernel
	./tools/echo
)
